Context of the x86-rems run
The configuration under which the translator ran, and every
interpretation that a model of the run uses. The Interpretations
section of backend/README.md explains each interpretation; a comment
at the top of a model lists what is specific to it.

Configuration
  initial-bool log_register_writes=false

Interpretations
  Each Sail call or construct is replaced by the HOL term below it. a,
  b, ... stand for its arguments, s for the state before it, s' for the
  state after it and s0 for the state at the start of the instruction.

  read_gpr(a)
    ~> read (registers :> (element (iword a))) s
  rflags
    ~> read reg_rflags s
  rflags = a
    ~> s' = write reg_rflags a s
  rip = a
    ~> s' = write reg_rip a s
  sail_shiftleft(a, b)
    ~> if ((& 0) <= b) then (word_shl a (num_of_int b)) else v, where
      the whole relation is ?v:16 word. ...
  sail_shiftleft(a, b)
    ~> if ((& 0) <= b) then (word_shl a (num_of_int b)) else v, where
      the whole relation is ?v:17 word. ...
  sail_shiftleft(a, b)
    ~> if ((& 0) <= b) then (word_shl a (num_of_int b)) else v, where
      the whole relation is ?v:8 word. ...
  sail_shiftleft(a, b)
    ~> if ((& 0) <= b) then (word_shl a (num_of_int b)) else v, where
      the whole relation is ?v:9 word. ...
  sail_shiftright(a, b)
    ~> if ((& 0) <= b) then (word_ushr a (num_of_int b)) else v, where
      the whole relation is ?v:16 word. ...
  sail_shiftright(a, b)
    ~> if ((& 0) <= b) then (word_ushr a (num_of_int b)) else v, where
      the whole relation is ?v:17 word. ...
  sail_shiftright(a, b)
    ~> if ((& 0) <= b) then (word_ushr a (num_of_int b)) else v, where
      the whole relation is ?v:8 word. ...
  sail_shiftright(a, b)
    ~> if ((& 0) <= b) then (word_ushr a (num_of_int b)) else v, where
      the whole relation is ?v:9 word. ...
  throw a
    ~> no final state
  undefined : int
    ~> v, where the whole relation is ?v:int. if (& 0) <= v then ...
      else no final state
  write_gpr(a, b)
    ~> s' = write (registers :> (element (iword a))) b s
